Inventory Analytics — Roberto Rossi (@cs-rossi: 0, is #reference, #part-of @cs-sources) { r_61Y17EAC05XZSS1B28NX17SV7C
Roberto Rossi. Inventory Analytics, Open Book Publishers, 2021, 184 pages, DOI 10.11647/OBP.0252. [Publisher and complete contents](https://www.openbookpublishers.com/books/10.11647/obp.0252) · [Publisher full text](https://books.openbookpublishers.com/10.11647/obp.0252.pdf) · [University-held publisher PDF](https://www.pure.ed.ac.uk/ws/portalfiles/portal/211432347/RossiOBP2021InventoryAnalytics.pdf) · [Library of Congress full-text copy](https://tile.loc.gov/storage-services/master/gdc/gdcebookspublic/20/20/44/74/93/2020447493/2020447493.pdf).

Read the whole book and work its mathematical/computational examples, including deterministic control, forecasting, stochastic inventory and multiple echelons. Preserve the assumptions behind each policy when adapting it to grades, release delays and aging chemicals.

The publisher identifies CC BY 4.0, publication 24 May 2021 and PDF ISBN 9781800641778; the indexed Library of Congress file preserves that notice. Metadata and complete chapter listing were checked on 29 October 2026. The publisher PDF returned 405; the university and 32,349,525-byte Library of Congress PDFs exceeded the browser's size limit. Full-page inspection is not claimed. External code and figures keep their own notices and remain outside this repository.

